ne of [:corroborated, :unfalsified, :disputed, :refuted].\\n     :empiricallyVerified is reserved for runner-executed test assertions; web text never carries it.\\n   - sourceKind: one of [:primaryArtifact, :peerReviewed, :crowdsourced, :secondaryReport, :unverifiedWeb].\\n5. Polarity:\\n   - isFalsifying: boolean (true or false).\\n   - At depth 'bipolar' or 'matrix' the facts hold at least one affirmative fact (:isFalsifying false) and at least one adversarial fact or limitation (:isFalsifying true).\\n6. A fact from a crawled web source ('crawled': true in Raw Evidence) carries :crawled true in its (:fact ...) form.\\n7. positiveSynthesis: 1-2 sentences summarizing what the facts support.\\n8. falsificationCritique: 1-2 sentences summarizing limitations, failure modes, counter-evidence, or edge cases the facts show.\\n9. summary: 2-3 sentence executive synthesis.\\n\\nFormat specification:\\n(:researchReport\\n  :topic \\\"Rust \\\\\\\"memory\\\\\\\" safety\\\"\\n  :summary \\\"...\\\"\\n  :positiveSynthesis \\\"...\\\"\\n  :falsificationCritique \\\"...\\\"\\n  :facts (\\n    (:fact :id \\\"fact-1\\\" :predicate (:relation \\\"verb\\\" :subject \\\"noun\\\" :object \\\"noun\\\") :claim \\\"...\\\" :evidence \\\"...\\\" :source \\\"https://...\\\" :sourceKind :primaryArtifact :verificationStatus :corroborated :crawled true :isFalsifying false)\\n    ...)\\n  :sources (\\\"https://...\\\" ...))\\n\\nRaw Evidence:\\n[\\n  {\\n    \\\"id\\\": \\\"item-1\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Page Title One\\\",\\n    \\\"snippet\\\": \\\"Rust uses ownership to manage memory without a garbage collector at all.\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://rust.example/1\\\",\\n    \\\"crawled\\\": true,\\n    \\\"sourceKind\\\": \\\"primaryArtifact\\\",\\n    \\\"isFalsifying\\\": false,\\n    \\\"tables\\\": [\\n      {\\n        \\\"cols\\\": [\\n          \\\"a\\\"\\n        ],\\n        \\\"rows\\\": [\\n          [\\n            \\\"1\\\"\\n          ]\\n        ]\\n      }\\n    ]\\n  },\\n  {\\n    \\\"id\\\": \\\"item-2\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Caf\\\\u00e9 \\\\ud83d\\\\ude00 \\\\\\\"q\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\",\\n    \\\"snippet\\\": \\\"GC pauses hurt latency in some Java workloads.\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://blog.example/2\\\",\\n    \\\"crawled\\\": false,\\n    \\\"sourceKind\\\": \\\"secondaryReport\\\",\\n    \\\"isFalsifying\\\": true,\\n    \\\"codeBlocks\\\": [\\n      {\\n        \\\"lang\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n        \\\"code\\\": \\\"x\\\\ty\\\"\\n      }\\n    ]\\n  },\\n  {\\n    \\\"id\\\": \\\"item-3\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": null,\\n    \\\"snippet\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"u\\\",\\n    \\\"score\\\": 0.1,\\n    \\\"n\\\": 3,\\n    \\\"e\\\": [],\\n    \\\"o\\\": {}\\n  }\\n]\"}")
(:case :id "p167" :kind "pure" :in "{\"fn\": \"research_prompt\", \"args\": [\"t\\\\opic\", \"flash\", [{\"id\": \"item-1\", \"title\": \"Page Title One\", \"snippet\": \"Rust uses ownership to manage memory without a garbage collector at all.\", \"url\": \"https://rust.example/1\", \"crawled\": true, \"sourceKind\": \"primaryArtifact\", \"isFalsifying\": false, \"tables\": [{\"cols\": [\"a\"], \"rows\": [[\"1\"]]}]}, {\"id\": \"item-2\", \"title\": \"Caf\\u00e9 \\ud83d\\ude00 \\\"q\\\" \\\\\", \"snippet\": \"GC pauses hurt latency in some Java workloads.\", \"url\": \"https://blog.example/2\", \"crawled\": false, \"sourceKind\": \"secondaryReport\", \"isFalsifying\": true, \"codeBlocks\": [{\"lang\": \"\", \"code\": \"x\\ty\"}]}, {\"id\": \"item-3\", \"title\": null, \"snippet\": \"\", \"url\": \"u\", \"score\": 0.1, \"n\": 3, \"e\": [], \"o\": {}}], true]}" :out "{\"value\": \"Research triage: the raw evidence below distils into one ASN S-expression, the (:researchTriage ...) form specified at the end.\\nA claim is weighed against primary-source evidence, and the evidence against it (failure modes, boundaries, negative tradeoffs, disconfirming sources) counts as much as the evidence for it.\\nThe reply is read by an ASN parser: parentheses only; markdown code fences, JSON, brackets and backticks make it unreadable.\\n\\nTopic: t\\\\opic\\nDepth: flash\\n\\nSchema:\\n1. verificationStatus is one of [:corroborated, :unfalsified, :disputed, :refuted].\\n   :empiricallyVerified is reserved for runner-executed test assertions; web text never carries it.\\n2. At depth 'bipolar' or 'matrix' the facts hold both polarities: at least one affirmative fact (:isFalsifying false) and at least one adversarial fact (:isFalsifying true).\\n3. Every fact has :predicate (:relation \\\"verb\\\" :subject \\\"noun\\\" :object \\\"noun\\\") whose subject is a specific thing the source states something about, never the whole topic, and an integer :srcRef into the :sources list.\\n4. A fact is a claim the source text states; a page title is not a fact.\\n\\nFormat specification:\\n(:researchTriage\\n  :topic \\\"t\\\\\\\\opic\\\"\\n  :facts (\\n    (:p :id \\\"fact-1\\\" :predicate (:relation \\\"verb\\\" :subject \\\"noun\\\" :object \\\"noun\\\") :srcRef 1 :verificationStatus :corroborated :isFalsifying false)\\n    (:p :id \\\"fact-2\\\" :predicate (:relation \\\"verb\\\" :subject \\\"noun\\\" :object \\\"noun\\\") :srcRef 2 :verificationStatus :disputed :isFalsifying true))\\n  :sources (\\\"https://example.com\\\" ...))\\n\\nRaw Evidence:\\n[\\n  {\\n    \\\"id\\\": \\\"item-1\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Page Title One\\\",\\n    \\\"snippet\\\": \\\"Rust uses ownership to manage memory without a garbage collector at all.\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://rust.example/1\\\",\\n    \\\"crawled\\\": true,\\n    \\\"sourceKind\\\": \\\"primaryArtifact\\\",\\n    \\\"isFalsifying\\\": false,\\n    \\\"tables\\\": [\\n      {\\n        \\\"cols\\\": [\\n          \\\"a\\\"\\n        ],\\n        \\\"rows\\\": [\\n          [\\n            \\\"1\\\"\\n          ]\\n        ]\\n      }\\n    ]\\n  },\\n  {\\n    \\\"id\\\": \\\"item-2\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Caf\\\\u00e9 \\\\ud83d\\\\ude00 \\\\\\\"q\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\",\\n    \\\"snippet\\\": \\\"GC pauses hurt latency in some Java workloads.\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://blog.example/2\\\",\\n    \\\"crawled\\\": false,\\n    \\\"sourceKind\\\": \\\"secondaryReport\\\",\\n    \\\"isFalsifying\\\": true,\\n    \\\"codeBlocks\\\": [\\n      {\\n        \\\"lang\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n        \\\"code\\\": \\\"x\\\\ty\\\"\\n      }\\n    ]\\n  },\\n  {\\n    \\\"id\\\": \\\"item-3\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": null,\\n    \\\"snippet\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"u\\\",\\n    \\\"score\\\": 0.1,\\n    \\\"n\\\": 3,\\n    \\\"e\\\": [],\\n    \\\"o\\\": {}\\n  }\\n]\"}")
